{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This chapter details Spring’s integration with third-party web frameworks."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "One of the core value propositions of the Spring Framework is that of enabling "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "choice"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". In a general sense, Spring does not force you to use or buy into any particular architecture, technology, or methodology (although it certainly recommends some over others). This freedom to pick and choose the architecture, technology, or methodology that is most relevant to a developer and their development team is arguably most evident in the web area, where Spring provides its own web frameworks ("
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Spring MVC"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "web/webmvc.html#mvc"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Spring WebFlux"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "web/webflux.html#webflux"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") while, at the same time, supporting integration with a number of popular third-party web frameworks."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Before diving into the integration specifics of each supported web framework, let us first take a look at common Spring configuration that is not specific to any one web framework. (This section is equally applicable to Spring’s own web framework variants.)"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "One of the concepts (for want of a better word) espoused by Spring’s lightweight application model is that of a layered architecture. Remember that in a \"classic\" layered architecture, the web layer is but one of many layers. It serves as one of the entry points into a server-side application, and it delegates to service objects (facades) that are defined in a service layer to satisfy business-specific (and presentation-technology agnostic) use cases. In Spring, these service objects, any other business-specific objects, data-access objects, and others exist in a distinct \"business context\", which contains no web or presentation layer objects (presentation objects, such as Spring MVC controllers, are typically configured in a distinct \"presentation context\"). This section details how you can configure a Spring container (a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") that contains all of the 'business beans' in your application."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Moving on to specifics, all you need to do is declare a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ContextLoaderListener"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/web/context/ContextLoaderListener.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the standard Jakarta EE servlet "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "web.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " file of your web application and add a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "contextConfigLocation"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<context-param/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " section (in the same file) that defines which set of Spring XML configuration files to load."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Consider the following "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<listener/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " configuration:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<listener>\n\t<listener-class>org.springframework.web.context.ContextLoaderListener</listener-class>\n</listener>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Further consider the following "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<context-param/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " configuration:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<context-param>\n\t<param-name>contextConfigLocation</param-name>\n\t<param-value>/WEB-INF/applicationContext*.xml</param-value>\n</context-param>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you do not specify the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "contextConfigLocation"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " context parameter, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ContextLoaderListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " looks for a file called "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/WEB-INF/applicationContext.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to load. Once the context files are loaded, Spring creates a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/web/context/WebApplicationContext.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " object based on the bean definitions and stores it in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ServletContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " of the web application."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "All Java web frameworks are built on top of the Servlet API, so you can use the following code snippet to get access to this \"business context\" "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " created by the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ContextLoaderListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows how to get the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext ctx = WebApplicationContextUtils.getWebApplicationContext(servletContext);"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "WebApplicationContextUtils"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/web/context/support/WebApplicationContextUtils.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class is for convenience, so you need not remember the name of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ServletContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute. Its "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "getWebApplicationContext()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method returns "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " if an object does not exist under the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext.ROOT_WEB_APPLICATION_CONTEXT_ATTRIBUTE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key. Rather than risk getting "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "NullPointerExceptions"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in your application, it is better to use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "getRequiredWebApplicationContext()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method. This method throws an exception when the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is missing."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Once you have a reference to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", you can retrieve beans by their name or type. Most developers retrieve beans by name and then cast them to one of their implemented interfaces."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Fortunately, most of the frameworks in this section have simpler ways of looking up beans. Not only do they make it easy to get beans from a Spring container, but they also let you use dependency injection on their controllers. Each web framework section has more detail on its specific integration strategies."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "web-integration-common",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Common Configuration"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JavaServer Faces (JSF) is the JCP’s standard component-based, event-driven web user interface framework. It is an official part of the Jakarta EE umbrella but also individually usable, for example, through embedding Mojarra or MyFaces within Tomcat."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Please note that recent versions of JSF became closely tied to CDI infrastructure in application servers, with some new JSF functionality only working in such an environment. Spring’s JSF support is not actively evolved anymore and primarily exists for migration purposes when modernizing older JSF-based applications."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The key element in Spring’s JSF integration is the JSF "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ELResolver"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " mechanism."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "SpringBeanFacesELResolver"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " is a JSF compliant "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ELResolver"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " implementation, integrating with the standard Unified EL as used by JSF and JSP. It delegates to Spring’s \"business context\" "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " first and then to the default resolver of the underlying JSF implementation."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Configuration-wise, you can define "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "SpringBeanFacesELResolver"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " in your JSF "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "faces-context.xml"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " file, as the following example shows:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<faces-config>\n\t<application>\n\t\t<el-resolver>org.springframework.web.jsf.el.SpringBeanFacesELResolver</el-resolver>\n\t\t...\n\t</application>\n</faces-config>"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "xml",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "jsf-springbeanfaceselresolver",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Spring Bean Resolver"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "A custom "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ELResolver"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " works well when mapping your properties to beans in "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "faces-config.xml"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ", but, at times, you may need to explicitly grab a bean. The "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "FacesContextUtils"
                          }
                        ],
                        "kind": "monospace",
                        "roles": []
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "link",
                    "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/web/jsf/FacesContextUtils.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " class makes this easy. It is similar to "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "WebApplicationContextUtils"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ", except that it takes a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "FacesContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " parameter rather than a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ServletContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " parameter."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The following example shows how to use "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "FacesContextUtils"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext ctx = FacesContextUtils.getWebApplicationContext(FacesContext.getCurrentInstance());"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "java",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "jsf-facescontextutils",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Using "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "FacesContextUtils"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jsf",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "JSF"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Invented by Craig McClanahan, "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Struts"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://struts.apache.org"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is an open-source project hosted by the Apache Software Foundation. Struts 1.x greatly simplified the JSP/Servlet programming paradigm and won over many developers who were using proprietary frameworks. It simplified the programming model; it was open source; and it had a large community, which let the project grow and become popular among Java web developers."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
